/**
 * @defgroup PhmdGeo PhmdGeo — Photon Multiplicity Detector Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Photon Multiplicity Detector
 *        (PMD/PHMD).
 *
 * @details
 * The PMD measures photon multiplicity and spatial distributions in the forward
 * pseudorapidity range 2.3 < η < 3.7 (west side of STAR).  It consists of two
 * planes of honeycomb proportional counters:
 *
 * - **CPV (Charged Particle Veto):** upstream plane at z = −539 cm; vetoes
 *   charged particles before the converter.
 * - **PMD (Preshower plane):** downstream plane at z = −550 cm, behind a
 *   3 X₀ lead converter (PARPBz = 0.75 cm half-thickness).
 *
 * Each plane is subdivided into three 120° sectors (@c PHMS), each filled with
 * rectangular supermodules of copper honeycomb cells.  The hexagonal cells have
 * an inscribed radius of 0.5282 cm and a gas depth of 0.8 cm (Ar/CO₂).  Cells
 * are grouped by the @c nx/@c ny (five module types) and @c mx/@c my (seven
 * supermodule sizes) arrays in the @c PMDG structure.
 *
 * The @c pmvr.config parameter (1 or 2) selects between two alternate
 * supermodule layout arrangements.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup PhmdGeoBase PhmdGeo — PMD geometry (configurations 1 and 2)
 * @ingroup PhmdGeo
 * @brief Module @c PHMDGEO: Honeycomb proportional counter array for photon
 *        multiplicity measurement.
 *
 * @details
 * Structures:
 * - @c PMVR — version and config selector (config = 1 or 2).
 * - @c PMDG — full geometry: mother-volume limits (m_min = 22 cm,
 *   m_max = 135 cm), z positions of two planes (zdist = {−539, −550} cm),
 *   box dimensions (DPMDx = DPMDy = 270 cm, DPMDz = 10 cm), layer
 *   thicknesses (PARGCz = 0.40 cm gas CPV, PARSCz = 0.40 cm gas PMD,
 *   PARFEz = 0.25 cm iron, PARPBz = 0.75 cm lead), cell dimensions
 *   (cell_radius = 0.5282 cm, cell_depth = 0.8 cm, cell_wall = 0.2 cm),
 *   passive layer thicknesses (th_lead = 1.5 cm, th_steel = 0.5 cm,
 *   th_pcb = 0.16 cm, th_base = 0.3 cm), and module-size arrays
 *   (nx/ny for 5 types; mx/my for 7 supermodule sizes).
 *
 * Volume hierarchy:
 * @c PHMD (box envelope) →
 * @c PHMS (sector, 3× at 120° steps) →
 * @c PHSR (detector box, air) →
 * @c PMDA (detector box, aluminium) →
 * @c AIRA (air interior) + @c PPBA (lead plates) + @c PFEA (iron frames) +
 * @c BASA (G10 base) + @c PCBA (PCB) →
 * @c PHCA (honeycomb plane) →
 * @c ASTR (cell row) →
 * @c PDCU (copper cell wall) + @c PDGS (active gas cell)
 * and @c PSTR (boundary pseudo-cell).
 *
 * Controlled by setups:
 * - @c PHMDof — detector off.
 * - @c PHMDon — default (config from Fill = 1).
 * - @c PHMD01 — pmvr.config = 1.0 (explicit).
 * - @c PHMD02 — pmvr.config = 2.0 (alternate layout).
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
